Dawn, Devra Leaves
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/relay_post]

FIXME(mundane): The storm has cleared in the night. First light is gray-pink across the mesa. Devra is at the door with her pack on her shoulder and your sealed letter in her hand. She slides the duplicate transcriptions into a wax-paper sleeve and tucks them inside her coat.

FIXME(dread): She does not say goodbye to Ossal. She does not look back at the wire. She steps out into the clearing dust and walks west toward Aldgate at a steady pace. You watch her until she is out of sight.

FIXME(dread): Ossal does not take Devra's departure well. He stands in the open doorway watching her go for a long minute. Then he starts cursing. He curses Devra by name, by family, by office. He swears a patrol will be on her by midday. He swears she will be back here in chains by sundown.

FIXME(dread): He turns the curses on you. He does not accuse you outright but he tells you what you already know: that letter did not write itself, that the guild chapter in Aldgate will receive whoever they receive, that there were two people in this post tonight who could write a guild credential and Devra was not one of them. He tells you not to speak a word of what happened here to anyone. He tells you he will remember your face. He is shaking.

FIXME(revelation): The wire ticks once in its cradle. Then again. Then it comes alive in a long sequence neither of you understands. Ossal stops mid-sentence and stares at it. He is an inspector. He has never sat the wire. He does not have the protocol fluent enough to transcribe in real time. The wire ticks on for half a minute and stops. Nobody has written anything down. The message is gone. Nobody knows what it said. Nobody will.

choices:

* Walk out into the morning = Take the road north and put the post behind you
    FIXME(mundane): You leave Ossal at the desk. Outside the air is clean for the first time in a day. The pennant on the pole has been torn half off by the storm and hangs limp in the new light.
    +finish_dungeon
    +add_level
